<!--
    A captured efrpg payload. WireContractTests uses it to prove the generator still agrees with the
    tool about what crosses the wire, now that the two live in separate repositories and no build
    sees both halves.

    Real efrpg output, not hand written XML. Produced against the SQL Server EfrpgTest database with
    the flags: database SqlServer, connection (EfrpgTest), stored-procedures, synonyms, multi-context,
    multi-context-connection-base64 (EfrpgTest_Settings). Then reduced to the smallest set of rows that
    still contains every attribute name and every element tag, topped back up with one row per distinct
    column typeName and per distinct stored procedure parameter dataType. One Errors row is merged in
    from a run where the MultiContext tables were absent, because a healthy run emits none.

    Regenerate whenever WireFormat.SchemaVersion is bumped, and copy the result to both repositories.
    A member added to a wire DTO that the tool was never taught to emit is exactly what this catches,
    so a failure means either the fixture is stale or the two sides have genuinely diverged.
-->
